# Optional. Leave unset for normal development.
#
# The app resolves its API base URL in this order:
#   1. A server URL saved in Settings inside the app — always wins
#   2. EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL below — an explicit build-time override
#   3. Metro's host — dev builds auto-follow the machine serving the bundle,
#      so the Inkwell server on that same machine needs no config
#   4. extra.lanHost — this machine's LAN address, recorded by app.config.js at
#      bundle time. Covers a build installed on a device, which has no Metro to
#      ask and would otherwise fall back to loopback (i.e. the phone itself).
#   5. extra.productionApiUrl in app.json — a real deployment
#   6. loopback — last resort, correct only in the iOS simulator
#
# Tiers 4 and 5 swap places depending on the build: a dev build prefers the LAN
# address, a release build prefers the configured production URL and keeps LAN
# only as a fallback — otherwise a shipped app would address the machine that
# built it.
#
# The PORT is not hardcoded either. app.config.js reads INK_PORT_BASE (or the
# legacy PCP_PORT_BASE) from the shell that started Metro, so an isolated
# server started with INK_PORT_BASE=4801 is reached with no change here.
#
# Set this only to aim a build at something other than the machine running
# Metro — a staging API, a colleague's box, a tunnel.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://inkwell.example.com
